## Commands & Syntax

### CICS Command Structure

All CICS commands follow this pattern:

```cobol
EXEC CICS command-name
  [WITH option1]
  [WITH option2]
  [RETURNING return-code]
END-EXEC.
```

### Common CICS Commands

#### 1. Terminal I/O Commands

```cobol
* SEND command - Send data to terminal
EXEC CICS SEND TEXT
  FROM(MESSAGE-TEXT)
  LENGTH(MESSAGE-LENGTH)
  ERASE
END-EXEC.

* RECEIVE command - Get data from terminal
EXEC CICS RECEIVE INTO(DATA-AREA)
  LENGTH(DATA-LENGTH)
  MAXLENGTH(MAX-DATA-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

* SEND MAP - Send formatted screen
EXEC CICS SEND MAP('MYMAP')
  MAPSET('MYMAPSET')
  FROM(MAP-AREA)
  ERASE
END-EXEC.

* RECEIVE MAP - Get formatted screen data
EXEC CICS RECEIVE MAP('MYMAP')
  MAPSET('MYMAPSET')
  INTO(MAP-AREA)
END-EXEC.
```

#### 2. Transaction Control Commands

```cobol
* SYNCPOINT (Commit)
EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
END-EXEC.

* ROLLBACK
EXEC CICS ROLLBACK
END-EXEC.

* RETURN - Return control to CICS
EXEC CICS RETURN
  TRANSID('NEXT-TRANS')
  COMMAREA(SHARED-AREA)
  LENGTH(AREA-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.
```

#### 3. File Control Commands

```cobol
* READ - Read record from file
EXEC CICS READ
  DATASET('FILENAME')
  INTO(RECORD-AREA)
  RIDFLD(KEY-VALUE)
  LENGTH(RECORD-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

* WRITE - Write record to file
EXEC CICS WRITE
  DATASET('FILENAME')
  FROM(RECORD-AREA)
  RIDFLD(KEY-VALUE)
  LENGTH(RECORD-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

* UPDATE - Modify existing record
EXEC CICS UPDATE
  DATASET('FILENAME')
  FROM(RECORD-AREA)
  LENGTH(RECORD-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

* DELETE - Remove record
EXEC CICS DELETE
  DATASET('FILENAME')
  RIDFLD(KEY-VALUE)
END-EXEC.
```

#### 4. Temporary Storage Commands

```cobol
* PUT into temporary storage
EXEC CICS PUT CONTAINER('TEMP-ITEM')
  FROM(DATA-AREA)
  LENGTH(DATA-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

* GET from temporary storage
EXEC CICS GET CONTAINER('TEMP-ITEM')
  INTO(DATA-AREA)
  LENGTH(DATA-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.
```

#### 5. Database (DB2) Commands

```cobol
* Execute SQL statement
EXEC CICS EXEC SQL
  SELECT * FROM CUSTOMERS
  WHERE CUST_ID = :CUST-ID
  INTO :CUSTOMER-ROW
END-EXEC.

* Prepare SQL
EXEC CICS PREPARE STATEMENT-NAME FROM SQL-STRING
END-EXEC.
```

#### 6. Exception Handling

```cobol
EXEC CICS READ
  DATASET('FILENAME')
  INTO(RECORD-AREA)
  RIDFLD(KEY-VALUE)
  NOT-FOUND
    MOVE 'Record not found' TO ERROR-MSG
  END-NOT-FOUND
  NOTAUTH
    MOVE 'Not authorized' TO ERROR-MSG
  END-NOTAUTH
  NOTOPEN
    MOVE 'File not open' TO ERROR-MSG
  END-NOTOPEN
END-EXEC.
```

