## Programming Models

### 1. Traditional CICS Programs

**Structure:**
```cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CUSTOMER-INQUIRY.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 CICS-COMMAREA.
   05 FUNCTION-CODE     PIC X.
   05 CUSTOMER-ID       PIC 9(8).
   05 CUSTOMER-NAME     PIC X(30).

PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CICS-COMMAREA.

MAIN-PROCEDURE.
    ACCEPT FUNCTION-CODE FROM SYSIN.
    
    IF FUNCTION-CODE = 'R'
        PERFORM READ-CUSTOMER
    END-IF.
    
    EXEC CICS SEND TEXT
        FROM(CUSTOMER-NAME)
        LENGTH(30)
    END-EXEC.
    
    EXEC CICS RETURN
        TRANSID('CUST')
        COMMAREA(CICS-COMMAREA)
        LENGTH(LENGTH OF CICS-COMMAREA)
    END-EXEC.
    
    STOP RUN.

READ-CUSTOMER.
    EXEC CICS READ
        DATASET('CUSTFILE')
        INTO(CUSTOMER-RECORD)
        RIDFLD(CUSTOMER-ID)
    END-EXEC.
```

### 2. Pseudo-Conversational Programming

**Concept:** Program invocation divided into steps

```
Step 1: RECV data → Process → SEND screen → EXIT
          ↓
Step 2: RECV data → Process → SEND screen → EXIT
          ↓
Step 3: RECV data → Process → SEND screen → EXIT
```

**Benefits:**
- Minimal memory per user
- Better scalability
- User think time doesn't block resources

### 3. CICS Services

Modern programming using CICS Services:

```cobol
CALL 'DFHEI1' USING
    EIBFN
    EIBDS
    EIBRESP
    EIBRESP2
    OTHER-PARAMS.
```

