## Transaction Management

### Transaction Life Cycle

```
1. INITIATION
   └─ User logs on
   └─ CICS creates task
   
2. PRESENTATION
   └─ Send initial menu/form
   
3. PROCESSING
   └─ User input received
   └─ Program logic executes
   └─ Database accessed
   
4. COMPLETION
   └─ Response sent to terminal
   └─ Transaction ends
   
5. CLEANUP
   └─ Resources released
   └─ Recovery log written
```

### Transaction States

```
┌─────────────────┐
│    Initiated    │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ↓
┌─────────────────┐
│   Suspended     │ (Waiting for resource)
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ↓
┌─────────────────┐
│    Running      │ (Active processing)
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ↓
┌─────────────────┐
│  Committing     │ (Writing changes)
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ↓
┌─────────────────┐
│   Terminated    │ (Completed)
└─────────────────┘
```

### Recovery & Restart

```
Failure Scenarios:
├─ System crash
│  └─ CICS restart reads recovery log
│  └─ Incomplete transactions rolled back
│  
├─ Program error
│  └─ Transaction abended
│  └─ Changes rolled back
│  └─ User notified
│  
└─ Deadlock detected
   └─ One transaction backed off
   └─ Retry mechanism activated
```

