## Performance & Optimization

### Performance Metrics

```
Key Performance Indicators (KPIs):

1. Response Time
   └─ Target: < 1 second for typical transaction

2. Throughput
   └─ Transactions per second

3. Resource Utilization
   └─ CPU, Memory, I/O

4. Availability
   └─ Target: 99.99% uptime

5. Error Rate
   └─ Target: < 0.1% transaction failures
```

### Optimization Techniques

#### 1. Pseudoconversational Design

```
Instead of:
SEND MENU
RECEIVE INPUT
PROCESS
SEND RESULT
(Blocking other users during think time)

Do:
SEND MENU → Return
(Next transaction)
RECEIVE INPUT → RETURN with transaction ID
(Next transaction)
PROCESS → SEND RESULT → Return
```

#### 2. Caching Strategy

```
Cache Levels:
├─ Program cache
│  └─ Keep in storage for reuse
│  
├─ Data cache
│  └─ Temporary storage for frequently accessed data
│  
└─ Map cache
   └─ Pre-compiled map definitions
```

#### 3. I/O Optimization

```
Techniques:
├─ Reduce file I/O operations
├─ Use VSAM with keys
├─ Batch operations where possible
├─ Use block I/O
└─ Optimize database queries
```

#### 4. Resource Management

```
CICS Resource Tuning:
├─ Task control blocks (TCBs)
├─ Storage pools (main storage, auxiliary)
├─ Buffer management
├─ File sharing optimization
└─ Message routing efficiency
```

