### Theory: ACID Compliance in Banking

```
Banking Transaction Requirements:

Atomicity:
├─ Transfer money = debit + credit
├─ Both must succeed or both must fail
└─ Never partial transfers

Consistency:
├─ Account balance always valid
├─ Total money in system preserved
└─ No orphaned transactions

Isolation:
├─ Other customers can't see pending transfers
├─ Concurrent transfers don't interfere
└─ Each transaction sees consistent data

Durability:
├─ Completed transfer survives any failure
├─ Logged to permanent storage
└─ Recoverable after system crash
```

